  - "cargo clippy --all-targets clean on the merged tree."
  - "The merge itself was verified as conflict-free in the direction that matters: git merge-tree --write-tree epic/redesign HEAD returns a bare tree hash with no CONFLICT line, so the WU -> epic merge no longer collides."
  - "The one conflict this sync produced was in docs/work/2026-09-04-redesign-plan.html's W7 row, where both branches recorded the same event from different vantage points. Resolved to the epic's landed prose plus W5's DEC-31 citation. Note git had ALREADY auto-merged the W8 row into exactly that shape, so the resolution follows a precedent set by the merge rather than a fresh judgement."
  - "Every pinned citation was checked to resolve, not assumed: git show ca18daa:ui/src/BodyViewer.tsx line 148 is the useState<Leg> per-flow default and 196-201 are the two leg ModeButtons — exactly what the eight citations claim."
